{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01415VdzbSVTRyF2uyrK4shD","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Debugging\n     2→\n     3→A cross-provider debugging skill for systematically diagnosing and resolving issues.\n     4→\n     5→## When to Use\n     6→\n     7→Use this skill when:\n     8→- A test failure or build error is unclear\n     9→- An agent is stuck in a loop or making no progress\n    10→- Runtime behavior doesn't match expectations\n    11→- You need to investigate state, logs, or configuration\n    12→\n    13→## Diagnostic Steps\n    14→\n    15→1. **Read the error message carefully.** Extract the file, line, and error type.\n    16→2. **Check recent changes.** Run `git diff` to see what changed since the last working state.\n    17→3. **Reproduce minimally.** Isolate the failing test or smallest reproduction case.\n    18→4. **Check logs and state.** Look for relevant log files, environment variables, or config issues.\n    19→5. **Search for similar patterns.** Use grep/find to locate related code or prior fixes.\n    20→6. **Fix and verify.** Apply the fix, run the failing test, then run the full test suite.\n    21→\n    22→## Common Failure Patterns\n    23→\n    24→| Symptom | Likely Cause | Investigation |\n    25→|---------|-------------|---------------|\n    26→| Import/module error | Missing dependency | Check go.mod / package.json / requirements.txt |\n    27→| Permission denied | File permissions or missing credentials | Check file modes and env vars |\n    28→| Test timeout | Deadlock or infinite loop | Add debug logging, check for blocking calls |\n    29→| Nil pointer / undefined | Uninitialized variable or missing return | Trace the call chain |\n    30→| Port already in use | Zombie process from previous run | Check `lsof -i :<port>` or `ss -tlnp` |\n    31→\n    32→## Debug Commands\n    33→\n    34→```bash\n    35→# Check process state\n    36→ps aux | grep <process-name>\n    37→\n    38→# Check listening ports\n    39→ss -tlnp | grep <port>\n    40→\n    41→# Check disk space\n    42→df -h\n    43→\n    44→# Check recent git changes\n    45→git log --oneline -10\n    46→git diff HEAD~1\n    47→\n    48→# Check environment\n    49→env | grep -i <keyword>\n    50→```\n    51→\n    52→## Scripts\n    53→\n    54→The `scripts/diagnose.sh` script automates common diagnostic checks.\n    55→Run it from the project root to get a quick health overview.\n    56→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01LjdhWd76AYp1fkFUM6hgcy","session_id":"340db9b5-d4b3-4f08-b063-55fbfbdb469b","uuid":"028ca504-a6ed-458d-9bcd-d2b0d72f28dc"}
